  "result": "The concept `drv.lane.entering_adjacent_lane` passed the gate (**OK**) on the first of the 6 allowed runs, with all three witnesses (holds, fails, blind) meeting their expected verdicts.\n\n**Body:** `st_lane_adjacency r1 s r2 ∧ (rel_occupies a r1 ∧ ¬rises (rel_occupies a r1)) ∧ rises (rel_occupies a r2)`\n\n- The formula language has no \"previous observation\" operator, so I wrote the \"previous observation\" part with `rises`:\n  - `rises (rel_occupies a r2)` means a overlaps r2 now and did not overlap it at the previous observation.\n  - `rel_occupies a r1 ∧ ¬rises (rel_occupies a r1)` means a overlaps r1 now and also did at the previous observation.\n- Because `rises` only fires on the first overlap, the concept holds once and not again until a leaves r2 and re-enters it from r1.\n- At a trace's first observation `rises` is unknown, and any unobserved occupancy or adjacency is unknown.\n\n**One behaviour to be aware of:** at the first observation of a trace, if a clearly does not overlap r2, the concept is false rather than unknown. The contract says \"no previous observation\" gives unknown, but under three-valued logic the missing previous observation can't change the result there. The accepted example concept (`u_turn_through_region`) behaves the same way, so I declared no narrowing and recorded this in the header and in `task_result.md`.\n\n**Witnesses:**\n- Two eastbound lanes 4 m wide: r1 = 100 and r2 = 101, with r2 recorded as r1's left neighbour, and s = left.\n- a is track 1, and each scenario is judged only at t = 1000 ms, so there is always a previous observation.\n- I supplied occupancy explicitly in each scene. In `holds`, a's centre sits exactly on the line between the lanes at the judged moment, and the builder's default only checks the centre point, so it would not register a footprint overlapping both lanes.\n\nOne shell command (two `grep`s chained together) was denied because it needed approval. A single `grep` that read the same Core definitions then ran fine, so nothing was lost.\n\nFiles are in `library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/lane/`, `library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/lane/`, and the working directory:\n- entering_adjacent_lane.lean (concept)\n- entering_adjacent_lane.lean (witnesses)\n- task_result.md",
